<title>GERMANY: VIAG Q1 pre-tax profit up at 674 mln dmk.</title>
<headline>VIAG Q1 pre-tax profit up at 674 mln dmk.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     674     vs 668</p>
<p>    Group sales				  12,300  vs 10,900</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German diversified utility is VIAG AG. In a mandatory bourse statement the group said that on an adjusted basis, to account for the extraordinary earnings from the sale of the Didier unit included in last year's numbers, the group's profits would have climbed by 7 pct. The group also said its specialty chemicals unit SKW Trostberg and utility Bayernwerk were largely responsible for the increase. The group said its pre-tax profit topped year ago levels despite start-up losses in the telecommunications business.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
